# Rails / sliders not working

Full playbook: `docs/rails-swiper.md`. Read it before changing rail options.

This has broken four times, each time differently. **Do not guess — inspect the
container's class list first**, it identifies the failure:

| Class list on `.swiper.subjects-swiper` | Failure |
|---|---|
| no `swiper-initialized` | Swiper never ran (load order / missing re-init) |
| `swiper-initialized`, nothing moves at all | stale instance after a Livewire morph |
| `swiper-initialized … swiper-css-mode`, touch works but mouse drag doesn't | `cssMode` removed Swiper's pointer gestures |

The console is **clean** in all three. "No console errors" ≠ "the JS is fine".

## Load-bearing — do not remove to fix a gesture

- `cssMode: true` in `app.js` — native `overflow-x` is the only thing that survives a
  Livewire morph. Swiper skips *all* its pointer handlers when this is on, which is why
  mouse drag needs the separate drag-to-scroll shim below it.
- `.rail-swiper.swiper-horizontal { touch-action: pan-x }` in `index.css` — Swiper's
  default `pan-y` blocks native horizontal scrolling on touch.
- `window.Swiper` comes from the prebuilt `public/assets/js/index.js`, loaded before
  `app.js` in the layout. Swiper is not an npm dependency; Vite is unrelated.

## Gesture matrix — re-check ALL of these after any rail change

Touch swipe, trackpad horizontal and shift+wheel are native. Mouse drag is the shim.
Plain vertical wheel intentionally does nothing (it would steal page scroll).

Every past fix repaired one gesture and silently killed another. Verify in a real
browser, not by reading code — `docs/rails-swiper.md` has a working headless-Chrome
recipe including how to mint a session cookie for the `auth:web` pages.
